 "hints": [
  "Read the message. With <code>%d</code> times 1, the stride is 1, and each device's part of the offset, <code>%e</code>, runs from 0 to 7. Slices of 1 element can't hold 8.",
  "Each device handles 2 blocks of 4 threads, 8 elements. So the device's part of the offset is <code>%d</code> times 8, which <code>%ds</code> already is.",
  "The load already uses the right offset, <code>%i</code> = <code>8d + 4b + t</code>. Store at it too: <code>%ov = shrink %o %i []</code>, and delete the <code>%j</code> line."
 ],
 "explain": "Each device runs 2 blocks of 4 threads, so it owns 8 elements: device <code>d</code> owns elements <code>8d</code> to <code>8d + 7</code>. The store must be at <code>d·8 + e</code> with <code>e</code> between 0 and 7, which is <code>%i</code>. The starter stored at <code>d + e</code>, a stride of 1, so device 0 and device 1 would both write elements 1 to 7."
}
